  "year": "1989",
  "subtitle": "The first flip phone, where the whole interface lives in an open/close gesture",
  "why_scout_cares": "The MicroTAC turned the mobile phone into a pocket object with a genuinely embodied interaction: the mouthpiece flips down over the keypad, so answering and dialing are one physical gesture and the device has a tactile open/close state. It is the direct physical-form-factor descendant of the museum's DynaTAC (1984) and the ancestor of every clamshell phone, yet no flip-phone exists in the collection. The flip/antenna ritual is a distinct embodied-interaction paradigm, not merely a smaller brick.",
  "search_terms": ["Motorola MicroTAC", "flip phone 1989", "first flip phone", "cellular phone clamshell", "MicroTAC 9800X"],
